This product uses the following separately licensed libraries, loaded
dynamically at run time and not modified:

- libsndfile (LGPL-2.1-or-later), https://libsndfile.github.io/libsndfile/
  bundled in the soundfile package's wheels. It reads and writes FLAC.
- Qt for Python (PySide6, shiboken6) and Qt, for the optional window and tray
  icon (the "gui" extra). They're offered under a choice of LGPL-3.0, GPL-2.0 or
  GPL-3.0; Signal Archive Recorder uses them under LGPL-3.0, as separately
  installed, dynamically loaded libraries. https://www.qt.io/qt-licensing

The Windows installer additionally bundles, as separate files in the program
folder:
- the Python runtime (PSF License) and the Python packages listed above, each
  with its own license file in the "licenses" folder;
- PortAudio (MIT), bundled in the sounddevice package's wheels;
- the PyInstaller bootloader (GPL-2.0 with a special exception that allows it to
  be distributed with programs under any license), https://pyinstaller.org.
Qt and libsndfile stay separate, replaceable DLLs, as the LGPL requires. The
installer itself is built with Inno Setup (https://jrsoftware.org/isinfo.php).
